From 6f5bdee2d5d5d1c545d5307f662d5e00e00536e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:42:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] graph leaves: context rANS leaf, codec 33, opt-in
 (KOLMO_NATIVE=rans)

With KOLMO_NATIVE=rans every graph leaf and every sub-stream of the format-2 leaves (21, 23) also
tries codec 33 and keeps it only when it is smaller than the leaf rule's choice; the IMG8 node
passes its row length and channel step so the residual leaf is coded under its neighbours'
magnitudes and the previous channel. Version 11 frames; the leaf is refused outside a graph
block and by decoders before it (rc3: 'corrupt or unsupported input'). No default output
changes: without the opt-in no frame holds the id. 'all' does not include 'rans'.

make check-krans: the coder's tests (plain and ASan/UBSan) and tests/test_krans_modes.py (every
mode, 1 and 4 threads, decoded without the opt-in). Added to check-rc.

Review R02, claim ctx-rans-leaf (#11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
